## 📊 Patient Intake & Priority Triage Workflow

Below is the interactive visual workflow mapping how I handle patient intake and triage upon arrival/telehealth check-in:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[📱 Patient Check-in / Call] --> B[📋 Patient Intake Form]
    B --> C{Verified Insurance & Demographics?}
    C -->|No| D[📞 Contact Patient for Missing Info]
    C -->|Yes| E[🏥 EMR Record Updated / Created]
    
    E --> F[🩺 Symptom & Chief Complaint Screening]
    F --> G{Triage Severity Assessment}
    
    G -->|Level 1 & 2: Emergent / Urgent| H[🚨 Immediate Physician Alert / Emergency Escalation]
    G -->|Level 3: Semi-Urgent| I[🟡 Queue for Same-Day Telehealth / Clinic Slot]
    G -->|Level 4 & 5: Routine / Non-Urgent| J[🟢 Standard Appointment Queue]

    H --> K[📝 Pre-Chart Documentation & SOAP Note Draft]
    I --> K
    J --> K
    K --> L[👨‍⚕️ Provider Consultation Ready]
